### Pruebas manuales (VS Code REST Client o Visual Studio / Rider)
@base = http://localhost:5000/api/reimbursements

### T01 - 100000 → Approved
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "employeeName": "Empleado Demo", "amount": 100000, "category": "Transporte", "description": "Taxi a reunión" }

### T02 - 500000 exactos → Approved
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "employeeName": "Empleado Demo", "amount": 500000, "category": "Alimentación", "description": "Almuerzo con cliente" }

### T03 - 500001 → Pending
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "employeeName": "Empleado Demo", "amount": 500001, "category": "Alimentación", "description": "Cena con cliente" }

### T04 - monto 0 → 400
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "employeeName": "Empleado Demo", "amount": 0, "category": "Otros", "description": "x" }

### T06 - descripción vacía → 400
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "employeeName": "Empleado Demo", "amount": 1000, "category": "Otros", "description": "   " }

### T08 - id inexistente → 404
GET {{base}}/999999

### T09 - filtro por estado
GET {{base}}?status=Pending

### T11 - filtros combinados
GET {{base}}?status=Pending&employeeName=Empleado%20Demo

### Estado inválido → 400
GET {{base}}?status=Foo

### T12 - aprobar (cambie el id por uno Pending)
PATCH {{base}}/3/approve

### T14 - rechazar sin motivo → 400
PATCH {{base}}/3/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "   " }

### T13 - rechazar con motivo (id Pending)
PATCH {{base}}/3/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "No cumple la política de gastos." }
